Below is what Brian said, which I do not quite understand. The problem
is the author is not responsive to any emails so it is not even clear
to us whether another person should take over these packages.

---

highlight uses snprintf, which is not part of C++, and depends on parser.

The final reminder about parser said:

'The immediate issue is that you are calling loadRcppModules without
having the package on the search path, and that Rcpp is so unwise as
to do

   description <- packageDescription(pkg)

without specifying lib.loc thereby assuming the package is on the
library search path (even though it insists it is called by .onLoad).'

---

Regards,
Yihui
