I wonder if we might ask Simon Urbanek, or Hadley or Uwe to please give the parser package a look-over.

Hopefully the fix is trivial, and one that they might be familiar with.  Once it gets over these new barriers to entry, it will set there happily with little to know watering or fertilizer, I am sure.

I worry in general that R is about of the age now where many packages will get orphaned like this as their developers move on in their lives... a better strategy ensuring enduring ownership is needed.

tim

