Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the short run, we can just fix the 'stderr' problem in 'parser' and
it should be good to come back on CRAN, but the problem in the long
run is more serious and may require more efforts. As far as I can see,
Romain copied lots of C code from bison and highlight
(http://www.andre-simon.de/doku/highlight/en/highlight.html), and I
really do not know what he did with all these C code. This is the
really messy part of maintaining parser and highlight.

Anyway, the most urgent thing is to get them back on CRAN, so can
someone take a look at how to fix the warning on 'stderr' during R CMD
check? It does not help by simply commenting out the lines which
contains 'stderr'. Romain has a script build-parser in the svn
repository, and if you want to hack at the parser package, you should
probably take that into consideration.

After parser is fixed, highlight should be easier since the current
problems are purely from R's side (documentation problems).

BTW, we also need to convince Brian to put them back when the problems
are gone; this may be more difficult than fixing the problems...

Regards,
Yihui
--
